# AutoHarp audio — do not "fix" these again

The glitchy click is a **discontinuity or render hitch**, not a short envelope. Attack sliders are not the fix. Attack 0 must not click.

## One instrument

It is one drone. Chord change = retune the same oscillators. Do **not**:
- copy a second "old chord" and crossfade/swap
- restart the envelope or slam `mEnv`/`mAmp` to 0
- call `applyChord` twice (quality then note each used to apply)

Store note + quality, apply **once** at the start of `process()`.

## Never jump the output

- Keep phase and filter on a live voice. Never `phase = 0` / `filt = 0` on a sounding slot.
- New voices start at a zero-crossing and `amp = 0`, then slew amp.
- Slew increment and amp. A saw at phase 0 is -1; that is a click if amp is already up.
- Apply UI chord/strum **on the audio thread at a buffer boundary**. Main must only enqueue.

## Audio thread

Write samples. No `MIDISend`, no `dispatch_async`, no graph rebuild. MIDI is queued; flush off-thread.

## Engine

Build once. Rotate/screenshot/system sounds must never `rebuild`, `connect`, `stop`, or `setActive(false)`. If the engine already stopped, only `start()`. Reconnect only if `start()` fails.
